vkd3d-proton: HB_VKD3D_METALFX_FSR=1 runs a game's FSR 3.1 upscaler on the driver's temporal upscale (MetalFX).

When the driver lists "hb-upscale" in driverInfo (KosmicKrisp with Highball's 0013, which runs it on MetalFX's temporal
scaler), the game's own FSR 3.1 upscaler is recorded as one upscale instead of its passes. The passes are recognized
without game-specific data: at pipeline creation the game's amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_dx12.dll (next to its executable,
read only, never loaded or replaced) is scanned for its DXBC containers, each one's HASH part and PSV0 bindings tell its
pass (prepare_inputs b0 t0-t2 u0-u4, accumulate b0 s1 t8 u0 u2, any other FSR 3.1 pass "other"; FSR 2 and FSR 4
containers are left out), and a compute pipeline whose DXIL hash is in that table is marked.

At dispatch, prepare_inputs gives color (t2), depth (t1), motion vectors (t0), the constants (b0) and the context: its
u0, an image the FSR context owns, so every FSR context gets its own scaler and history. The passes after it are
dropped up to accumulate; prepare_reactivity, which has accumulate's binding shape but does not read the game's color,
gives the reactive mask when the game sets one. Accumulate becomes the upscale: into its output (u1), or, when the
game sharpens and u1 is not bound, into the upscaled color (u0) that the game's RCAS reads, so RCAS runs as the game
ships it with the game's sharpness, and nothing depends on recognizing RCAS. Everything after accumulate runs as
shipped. If the inputs or constants cannot be read, every pass runs as shipped.

The upscale is a vkCmdBlitImage2 from the color image's rendered region to the whole output, with a
VkHbTemporalUpscaleInfo (include/private/vkd3d_hb_upscale.h, Highball's own interface) in VkBlitImageInfo2's pNext
chain, which Wine passes to the driver as it is, between a barrier before (all earlier writes before the blit) and
one after (the blit's writes before everything later). A driver that cannot take the blit performs an ordinary blit.
FSR 3.1's constants carry only the ratio of this frame's pre-exposure to the last one's (deltaPreExposure), so the
pre-exposure passed is the product of those ratios since the context's last reset, kept for the last four contexts.
No exposure texture is passed: FSR's exposure resource is its own frame-information texture unless the game gives
one, and the luminance pass that writes it is one of those dropped. The compute root CBVs that are saved to read
the constants, and the FSR state, are cleared when the command list is reset, and the CBVs when the compute root
signature changes.

Without "hb-upscale" the switch logs once and the game's FSR runs as shipped. HB_VKD3D_METALFX_FSR=log only logs the
bindings. Optional switches: HB_FSR_MFX_AUTO_EXPOSURE (0), _REACTIVE (1), _DEPTH_REVERSED (1), _HIRES_MV (0, motion
vectors at the output size; needs a driver that supports them, KosmicKrisp only with the macOS 27 SDK and runtime).

Checked on an M5 Max, macOS 27.2 (2026-11-19), x86-64 build of this series with KosmicKrisp 0011 to 0013 built as in
CI: Forza Horizon 6 logs 301 FSR 3.1 shaders in its provider, "accumulate writes ... (the upscaled color the game's
RCAS sharpens)", and "kk: MetalFX temporal 1728x1117, content 1152x744 -> 1728x1117" at FSR Quality (3456x2234 at
Retina); full frame, the game's sharpening and HDR, no visible artifacts. No frame time against stock FSR, and no second
FSR 3.1 game tried yet.

Written for Highball from the FidelityFX SDK's public pass and binding layout and Vulkan; it shares no code with
MetalSharp (an earlier version of this patch followed MetalSharp's d3d12_command_list_metalfx_scale, AGPL-3.0, and was
replaced).

Upstream: not sent.

